 "observations": [
  "The page number «148» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the left the number of the table, «Tab. 37», in bold sans serif, underlined. The page has no signature. The titles (L01-L03), in bold, the sigla in roman; L03, the place of Jupiter's node, in smaller bold type, «2 S. 22 G. 1 M.», with note 1, as on p. 147 (JP2 0179). The folios of the manuscripts stand at the left of the last two titles, «C 61r, O 118v,» and «N 13v.», the letters raised; here as left margin notes.",
  "The table: rules and heads as on p. 147 (JP2 0179), with «Pagina numerorum (O) Semita numeri (C)» over the four columns of the arguments, divided below a rule into «Augmentum proprietatum omnium2)» and «Diminutio proprietatum omnium3)» in smaller type; «Sublimatio ascensus Jovis examinata4)»; «Examinatio ipsius elheza5)» and «Examinatio centri», each hyphenated «Exami-natio»; «Statio prima Jovis»; «Latitudo Jovis descendentis6)» over «prima» and «secunda» in smaller bold type. Here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L04-L08), the cells separated by our «|»; a head followed by empty cells spans their columns. L09, the units, in bold; the point after «Min» of the Statio prima is printed small, 3 px against the 6 px of the other points, and is transcribed.",
  "L10-L39. Checked as on p. 144 (JP2 0176): the Sublimatio is 5s 22° 32′ less half the Examinatio argumenti in every row, a half minute counted as a whole. The Latitudo secunda is 2° 30′ · sin x to within 0.6″ in every row except at 135° (L24): there 1° 45′ 4″ is 1′ less than 2° 30′ · sin 135° = 1° 46′ 4.0″, the 1° 46′ 4″ of p. 145 (JP2 0177) at 45°; its steps from 134° and to 136°, 2′ 50″ and 52″, stand against about 1′ 50″ and 1′ 52″. No note of the apparatus bears on the 45. At 122° and 139°, 2° 7′ 12″ and 1° 38′ 25″ agree with the computation, 2° 7′ 12.4″ and 1° 38′ 24.5″, where p. 145 has 2° 7′ 19″ at 58° and 1° 38′ 22″ at 41°.",
  "L10-L39. The Examinatio argumenti agrees with the equation of the epicycle of radius 11.3 of pp. 144-147 to within 1′ from 121° to 138°, and is larger from 139° on, by 1.2′ at 139° rising to 6.8′ at 150° (6° 32′ for 6° 25.2′); the steps of the column, 8′ to 10′ a degree, are regular, and the Sublimatio follows its values. The Examinatio centri for 180° − y is that of y on pp. 144-145 (JP2 0176-0177) except from 121° to 125° and at 132°, where it is 1′ smaller.",
  "L10-L39, the other columns: the Statio prima increases from 4s 6° 25′ to 4s 6° 59′, by 1′ to 3′ a degree to 125° and then by 1′ a degree (2′ from 131° to 132°). The Latitudo prima is 1° 10′ to 128° and decreases by 1′ every fourth degree, to 1° 4′ at 149° and 150°.",
  "Notes on the readings. Note 1: as on p. 147 (JP2 0179), the title of the node is N's; O has none, and C has 2. 12. 1. Notes 2-3: O's heads, «Augmentum computationis et numeri et diminutio examinis» and «Diminutio computationis et numeri et augmentum examinis», use the words of the heads of the arguments of Tab. 21-26 («Computatio minuenda et augmentum examinis et numeri», p. 136, JP2 0168). Note a: the last argument, 5s 0°, is N's; C and O have 4. Checked: the Sublimatio 5s 18° 14′ at 136° (note b, C and O, against N's 4) and 5s 18° 34′ at 141° (note c), each 5s 18° 13½′ and 5s 18° 33½′ by the rule, a half minute counted as a whole; the Examinatio centri 3° 31′ at 136° (note d) and 3° 15′ at 140° (note e), the value of p. 145 at 40°; the seconds 21 of the Latitudo secunda at 124° and 126° (note f), 2° 4′ 21.3″ and 2° 1′ 21.2″ computed.",
  "L30, «34e)», the Sublimatio at 141°: the apparatus has no note e for it; note c, «34] ON, 33 C», is its note, and note e, «15] ON, 12 C», belongs to the «15e)» of L29: see the critical note. N05: «ON,12 C.» with no space after the comma. Italics: «om.». N01-N03: the ellipses «. . . .» of the lemmata as printed. N01, «M]» and «omnium],»: see the critical notes."
 ],
